WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.113 --> 00:00:01.860
(rolls tongue) Rossy, what's next?

2
00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.460
All right. Up next, a writer in Vogue

3
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:05.800
recently explored this interesting question.

4
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.540
What if your friends don't like your partner?

5
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:09.627
Uh-oh.
Ooh.

6
00:00:09.627 --> 00:00:11.650
For some, it could be a total deal breaker.

7
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.650 line:15%
They'll just cut loose a lover

8
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:14.730 line:15%
if they can't vibe with their friends,

9
00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:16.690 line:15%
but on the other end of this spectrum,

10
00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:19.290 line:15%
some say they actually prefer a healthy separation

11
00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:20.530 line:15%
between their partner and their friends,

12
00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:23.110 line:15%
'cause it helps 'em see all sides of themselves.

13
00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:24.695 line:15%
Here's the deal, right?

14
00:00:24.695 --> 00:00:26.760 line:15%
(laughs) What?

15
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.650 line:15%
There is a choice you have to make.

16
00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.590 line:15%
If your friends tell you they don't like your partner

17
00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:33.550 line:15%
you have to think are they seeing something I'm not seeing?

18
00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.320 line:15%
Or is my relationship with them more important

19
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.840 line:15%
than my relationship with my partner?

20
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:39.780 line:15%
And I don't think there's a rule for everybody,

21
00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.150 line:15%
it's gotta be case by case.

22
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:42.248 line:15%
What do you think?

23
00:00:42.248 --> 00:00:43.733 line:15%
(audience applauds)
I agree with that.

24
00:00:46.141 --> 00:00:48.587 line:15%
How many people here would be honest and just be like,

25
00:00:48.587 --> 00:00:51.390
"I'm just not gelling with your partner."

26
00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.417
How many people would actually be honest and say that?

27
00:00:53.417 --> 00:00:54.920
(audience whoops)

28
00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:56.440
I like it.

29
00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:57.273
Not that many.

30
00:00:57.273 --> 00:00:59.690
How many people would just quietly bite it

31
00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:02.748
and kind of drift a little bit apart.

32
00:01:02.748 --> 00:01:03.840
(applause ripples)
Show the hands,

33
00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.578
If you don't mind. I love it.

34
00:01:05.578 --> 00:01:08.440
Why were you giggling up there?

35
00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:10.600
Yeah I mean, you have to be honest

36
00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:13.050
and also to not ruin everything,

37
00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:14.770
so it's difficult.

38
00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:16.416
You ruined everything.

39
00:01:16.416 --> 00:01:18.040
(all laugh)

40
00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:19.180
Say that, what...?

41
00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.617
I believe I heard a voice that said something about

42
00:01:21.617 --> 00:01:23.960
"You ruined everything."
(audience laughs)

43
00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.290
Wait, please, please.

44
00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:27.250
What, what did he ruin?

45
00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:31.470
Two days ago, I asked him to marry me

46
00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:33.663
on the Brooklyn Bridge,

47
00:01:34.536 --> 00:01:38.073
and he said to me, "Oh no, it's embarrassing, get up."

48
00:01:38.073 --> 00:01:41.023
(audience exclaim)
Yes you did that.

49
00:01:42.967 --> 00:01:44.599
No.

50
00:01:44.599 --> 00:01:47.266
(audience jeer)

51
00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:51.805
Okay, what does this have to do with a friend?

52
00:01:51.805 --> 00:01:53.124
(audience laughs awkwardly)

53
00:01:53.124 --> 00:01:54.007
Nothing.

54
00:01:54.007 --> 00:01:55.080
Nothing.
Nothing.

55
00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:58.106
Sorry, but I had to do this.

56
00:01:58.106 --> 00:01:59.040
(audience laugh awkwardly)

57
00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.793
Now what?

58
00:02:00.793 --> 00:02:03.335
Because I wanted to do it myself.

59
00:02:03.335 --> 00:02:04.210
Aw.

60
00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:05.043
Later.

61
00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:07.449
But not today.

62
00:02:07.449 --> 00:02:10.282
(audience laughs)

63
00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:15.473
No, we'll save it for an intimate moment.

64
00:02:15.473 --> 00:02:17.210
Aw.

65
00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:19.938
I'm getting the sense you don't like a crowd.

66
00:02:19.938 --> 00:02:21.543
(audience laughs)
Right?

67
00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.594
That was an emotional rollercoaster.

68
00:02:25.594 --> 00:02:26.427
(audience applauds)

69
00:02:26.427 --> 00:02:29.010 line:15%
(bright music)

